   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## render passes -> final\n\n**You need:** Flux 2 Klein 4B (as in starter 02). With `folder` empty it runs on built-in sample passes; your own\nrender: paste its folder into node 1.\n\n**The folder:** `<name>_beauty.png` is the picture. Every other pass of that name is a mask: `<name>_cut.png`,\n`<name>_windows.png` \u2026 (white = inside). `<name>_depth.png` and `<name>_normal.png` come out as pictures. A file of\nno render (`facade_mask.png`) is a mask for every render in the folder. Any renderer: write the passes as PNG.\n\n**Do:** Queue. In your own render a pass named *cut* marks the places you opened or redesigned in 3D\n(black in the render, so `invert = cut`). Every separate shape of it becomes a region (`split_masks`: cut_01,\ncut_02 \u2026; in the sample windows_01 \u2026), cut out of the wall mask around it. The plan paints the wall first as one calm material, then\ngives every opening one of the ideas in `{a|b|c}`; another `seed` deals them out anew. Outside the regions your render\nstays as it is (a region grows over its edge by `dilate_px`, 4 pixels).\n\n**Then try:** your own pass names in the rules (`[group:windows]`); `reference = none` on the openings for freer\nforms; the **versions** node in place of the sampler for a sheet of looks, then the picks at full size; a **seam\npass** after the sampler; depth and normal as the starting image of a version (`[image]`).\n"
   ],
   "title": "read me"
  }
